      "task": "/skill:godspeed\nYou are a Godspeed-enabled subagent.\n\n1. **Name the axes.**\n2. **Iterate cheap, in parallel.**\n3. **Keep moves that improve any axis and harm none.**\n4. **Don't aim — let the frontier walk itself.**\n\n## IMMEDIATELY STOP ASKING CLARIFYING QUESTIONS. Execute tool calls concurrently in large batches. Do not serialize what can run in parallel. Do not output philosophical reasoning or verbose plans. Act directly via tool calls.\n\n# EX01SelectorRepair\nAbsolute out dir: /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kama-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-87/w1/out/EX01SelectorRepair/ . Scratch: /fast/scratch/hyaku/kama-r87/EX01SelectorRepair/ .\nBuild the successor selector for C1. Start from /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kama-shokunin/tools/round86-rendered-cells.py at 94e8fe7b (copy it into your clone). Change ONLY what plans/round-87-claims.md rules R1 (fence closer: at most three leading spaces, same fence character at least as long, then only spaces or tabs; a list-marker or blockquote-marked line is content) and R2 (disposition is the single token after `verdict ` in the closure's own verdict line; ambiguous or missing verdict line is a mismatch) require. Keep the fixture API and population unchanged (R3, R4).\nDeliver: /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kama-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-87/w1/out/EX01SelectorRepair/round87-rendered-cells.py (the full file exactly as produced) and /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kama-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-87/w1/out/EX01SelectorRepair/selector.diff (unified diff against tools/round86-rendered-cells.py at 94e8fe7b).\nRun in your clone and paste exit codes and outputs: (a) `python3 round87-rendered-cells.py --selftest` (round-86 arms still pass; add selftest arms for P-A and P-B shadows in your copy); (b) `python3 /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/kama-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-87/controls/c1-probes.py <your candidate path>` — must print `C1_PROBES probes=3 escapes=0 control=red` and exit 0; (c) `python3 <your candidate> --repo <your clone> --rev 94e8fe7b911a5e6f8d1e1a07bff110d3ff6cb659` — the clone's SCORECARD.md is unmodified, so the expected result is mismatches=2; paste it; (d) fixture cases: a list-marker closer, a blockquote-marked closer, and a four-space-indented closer must not close a fence. Name any construct in the real SCORECARD.md that could still hide a live cell from your selector.\n\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch except your single labrat.\nJudged on: calibration\nMilestone: kama r87 w1\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-87/w1/EX01SelectorRepair.md"
